1
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:22,000
The life you live is the story you tell.

2
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Val is a documentary film directed by Leo Scott.

3
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:54,000
For over 40 years Val Kilmer, one of Hollywood’s most mercurial and/or misunderstood
actors has been documenting his own life and craft through film and video.

4
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:10,000
He has amassed thousands of hours of footage, from 16mm home movies made with his brothers, to time spent in
iconic roles for blockbuster movies like Top Gun, The Doors, Tombstone, and Batman Forever.

5
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:26,000
This raw, wildly original and unflinching documentary reveals a life lived to extremes and a
heart-filled, sometimes hilarious look at what it means to be an artist and a complex man.

6
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:42,000
Self, played by Val Kilmer.

7
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:58,000
Self / Narrator, played by Jack Kilmer.

8
00:58:08,000 --> 00:58:14,000
Self, played by Mercedes Kilmer.

9
01:05:24,000 --> 01:05:30,000
Self, played by Joanne Whalley.

10
01:12:40,000 --> 01:12:46,000
Val is a 2021 American documentary film directed and
produced by Leo Scott and Ting Poo.

11
01:19:56,000 --> 01:20:02,000
It follows the life and career of actor Val Kilmer.

12
01:27:12,000 --> 01:27:18,000
The film had its world premiere at the Cannes Film Festival on July 7, 2021, and was released in a limited
release on July 23, 2021, prior to digital streaming on Prime Video on August 6, by Amazon Studios.

13
01:34:28,000 --> 01:34:34,000
The film explores themes of biography, home movie footage,
archive footage, struggling actor, family photo.

14
01:41:44,000 --> 01:41:50,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
